<.shell current={:detail_list}>
  <h1>Detail list</h1>
  <p class="lead">Key facts about one record.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Kind</dt>
      <dd><.activity_badges activity={hd(activities())} /></dd>
      <dt>Attendance</dt>
      <dd>14 members · 62h 15m in total</dd>
      <dt>Start</dt>
      <dd>
        {Service.Format.datetime_medium(hd(activities()).started_at, sample_team().timezone)}
      </dd>
      <dt>Finish</dt>
      <dd>
        {Service.Format.datetime_medium(hd(activities()).finished_at, sample_team().timezone)}
      </dd>
      <dt>Actions</dt>
      <dd>
        <ul id="detail-list-actions" class="action-list">
          <li>
            <.a href="#">Change activity</.a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <.a href="#">Change tags</.a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <.a href="#">Send reminders</.a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <.a href="#">Mileage report</.a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <.a href="#" external={true}>Open in D4H</.a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h2>Custom fields</h2>
  <p>
    A record's custom fields, the ones its team or organization added, aren't in its sidebar: a BC incident has 27, which
    would push Actions 3 screens down. They're the record's Fields <a href={page_path(:tabs)}>tab</a>, a table with each
    field's name beside its value (decided 2026-10-28, #705). A required field left empty shows Missing to team admins on a
    draft incident, which can't be published until it's filled in. The missing ones come first, under a count, and the tab
    counts them too.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <.custom_fields_table id="detail-list-fields" rows={custom_field_rows()} required={19} />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>The facts at the top of a record's page, a label and a value each.</p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>Many records side by side. Use a <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>.</p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>A plain <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>. Each <code>dd</code> gets a rule under it.</p>
  <p>
    Custom fields are <code>&lt;.custom_fields_table&gt;</code>
    with rows from <code>CustomField.rows/4</code>, or <code>&lt;.custom_fields&gt;</code>
    under a heading on a page with no tabs, such as Your membership's Contact details.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every record's sidebar runs in the same order: its facts, then Actions. A count the main column
    already shows, such as a group's members, stays out of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Things to do with the record go last, under Actions, as a
    <code>&lt;ul class="action-list"&gt;</code>
    of links. Each link fills its row, so the whole row takes a tap. On a touch screen each row is 44px tall.
  </p>
  <p>
    Actions run in the same order on every record, so a link is where you left it on the last one. A page shows only
    the ones it has:
  </p>
  <ol class="list-decimal list-inside paragraph">
    <li>
      Change the record: Change activity, Change item, or Rename, then Change fields, Change tags, and Apply a template.
    </li>
    <li>Send: Send reminders, Send an update, Send attendance.</li>
    <li>Reports and other pages about the record, such as Mileage report.</li>
    <li>Open in D4H.</li>
    <li>Delete, last, away from Change.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A hint that stands in for an action, such as a published activity's tags, takes that action's place. In the app:
    <code>Web.ActionOrderTest</code>
    checks every Actions list.
  </p>
  <p>
    Change and Rename open a page of their own. Delete stays on the record's page: it opens the <a href={
      page_path(:confirm_dialog)
    }>confirm dialog</a>, which says what goes with it, and goes back
    to the list once it's done. In the app: <code>phx-click="delete"</code>
    with the attributes from <code>Web.DeleteConfirm</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
